      ]
    },
    "note": "Directorial federal republic. The seven-member Federal Council is collectively head of state and government; its members are elected individually by the Federal Assembly (both chambers in joint session) for four-year terms after each National Council election, and by-elections fill vacancies. The President of the Confederation is a Federal Councillor elected by the Federal Assembly for one year and is first among equals. The seats were shared 2 FDP, 2 CVP, 2 SP and 1 SVP (the 'magic formula') from 1959 to 2003."
  },
